Confirmed: `validate_pr` failure → log + `continue` — with overfetch, the loop naturally advances to the next candidate. The loop-level fallthrough works for both localActions and workflow dispatches; only the query slice starves them. The fix centers on:

1. `githubSource.queryPrs`: overfetch `limit + 3` + parked-tier void.
2. `smAgent.triggerWorkflow` catch: classify + record marker + park at cap (for PR-carrier items).

Now — one more check: the loop `break` conditions with localAction rules. `budgetCapped` excludes localActions → effectiveLimit = ruleLimit. Loop breaks at processedKeys >= ruleLimit. Failed localActions don't push processedKeys → next candidate processed in same tick. ✓ (for limit:1 → 1 success or all-fail walk).

Wait — there's one more thing to verify for the fallthrough test with the triggerWorkflow path: `if (triggered && !ruleSelfManagesLabel) addRuleLabels(key, ...)`. addRuleLabels → github_add_labels via tracker (jira tracker for github items? removeRuleLabel/addRuleLabels use githubTracker for github-source items?). Not relevant for failures.

Now, let me also think: does my change to queryPrs overfetch break the `machineSmAgent` or other consumers of githubSource.query? grep usage: smAgent (via sourceResolver), tests. The mergeBot doesn't use queryPrs. OK.

One more design point — the ask's item 1: "skip it with a recorded reason and continue down the FIFO — the slot goes to the next candidate in the same tick". The "recorded reason": marker comment (durable) + the existing console.warn (tick log). For non-no-ref errors: log-only (transient — a PR comment per rate-limit blip would be spam). I'll classify:
- `no-ref` (non-retryable): message matches /no ref found/i or /\b422\b/ or /ref.*not found/i? Careful: "422" appears in merge-conflict errors too (e.g. retryMergePR checks 422 for blocked). But here the context is triggerWorkflow dispatch errors only. GitHub's workflow_dispatch on missing ref: 422 "No ref found for: refs/<ref>". Also 404 "Not Found" for a missing workflow file... a missing workflow file is a deployment bug — not head-specific; parking a PR for it would be wrong (ALL PRs fail equally). Should 404 count? The ticket: "422 no-ref, or any non-retryable dispatch error". A missing workflow yml is non-retryable but NOT head-specific — parking every PR validation_failed would be catastrophic. So scope the park-counting to REF-class failures: /no ref found/i primarily. I'll classify: 'no-ref' if /no ref found/i OR (/422/ AND /ref/i). Everything else 'transient'. Transient → fallthrough + log, no marker/park.

Let me write it:

```js
function classifyTriggerError(message) {
    var s = String(message || '');
    if (/no ref found/i.test(s)) return 'no-ref';
    if (/\b422\b/.test(s) && /ref/i.test(s)) return 'no-ref';
    return 'transient';
}
```

Marker line (following the zombie format, grep-able):
`\u26A0\uFE0F trigger-failed <sha> — attempt N/cap at <iso>`
regex: `/\u26A0\uFE0F trigger-failed ([0-9a-f]{7,40}) \u2014 attempt (\d+)\/\d+ at (\S+)/g`

marks(bodies) → { sha: maxN }.

Also expose `capOf(jobParams)` → jobParams.triggerFailParkCap default 3, 'false'/0 disables parking (but markers still posted? if cap disabled → no counting → treat every failure as attempt ∞? Simpler: cap disabled → no marker, no park — log only).

Hmm wait — cap default 3: the ticket says "After N consecutive trigger failures one head (suggest 3)". So the THIRD failure parks. Marker shows attempt 1/3, 2/3, then 3/3 = park. My park logic: prior count >= cap - 1 → this failure is the cap-th → park (and the park comment itself records attempt cap/cap? I'll include the marker line with attempt cap/cap in the park comment for the audit trail).

Now write the pure module js/common/triggerFailures.js. Also — should the marker/post/park logic live in smAgent (side effects) with the pure parts (classify/regex/line/cap) in the module? Yes — module pattern matches validationLiveness ("pure functions, no tool globals — smAgent wires the transport").

One more consideration — `item.labels` for the already-parked guard: item.labels are PR labels (queryPrs). The parked guard: if labels include validation_failed → log-only. Also if the PR got parked by another rule between query and dispatch — the guard uses the queried labels (stale by one tick worst case; a duplicate park comment is possible but the label-add is idempotent and the marker post is bounded... acceptable; the fail_validation paths have the same race).

